repugnancy.d:
n. The state or condition of being repugnant; opposition;
   contrariety; especially, a strong instinctive antagonism; aversion;
   reluctance; unwillingness, as of mind, passions, principles, qualities,
   and the like.

rhapsodist.d:
n. Anciently, one who recited or composed a rhapsody;
   especially, one whose profession was to recite the verses of Hormer and
   other epic poets.
n. Hence, one who recites or sings poems for a livelihood;
   one who makes and repeats verses extempore.
